The 7th Commandment:


Thou shalt not steal!


The thief is considered one of the most despicable creatures. Anyone who takes something from another person without their consent is a thief!


Therein lies the explanation. In order to follow the commandment correctly, all a person has to do is always to clearly distinguish what belongs to another! That is not difficult, everyone will immediately say. And that is the end of it.


Of course, it is not difficult, just as all of the Ten Commandments are not difficult to follow if you really want to. But the condition is always that the person knows them properly. And many people lack that .


In order to comply, have you ever really thought about what is actually the other person's property and what you are not allowed to take from them?


That is his money, his jewelry, his clothes, perhaps also his house and farm with livestock and everything that goes with it. But the commandment does not say that it only concerns material earthly goods! There are values ​​that are far more precious!


A person's property also includes his reputation, his public image, his thoughts, his personality, and also the trust he enjoys from others, if not from all, then at least from this or that one!


Once we have reached this point, some people's pride will become a little more fainthearted in the face of the commandment. Ask yourself: Have you never tried, perhaps in good faith, to shake or completely undermine the trust that one person enjoys by admonishing them to be cautious? In doing so, you have literally stolen from the person to whom this trust was given! Because you have taken it from him, or at least made an attempt to do so.


You have also stolen from your neighbour if you know something about his circumstances and pass on this knowledge without the consent of the person concerned . From this you can see how deeply entangled in the web of guilt all those people are who try to make a business out of such things or who do business of this kind.


The self-entanglement in this, through all the consequences of this activity of constant violations of God's law, draws such a huge net that these people can never get out of it; for they are often more heavily burdened than physical burglars and thieves. Those who support and encourage such "businessmen" in their sinful trade are guilty and equal to fences.


Every honest and upright person, whether a private citizen or a business person, has the right and the duty to demand direct clarification and, if necessary, documentation from anyone who approaches him with any request, from which he can decide to what extent he can confidently fulfill the person's wishes. Anything else is unhealthy and reprehensible.


The fulfillment of this commandment also has the effect that the senses awaken more and more and their abilities are developed and exposed. Man thus gains the true knowledge of human nature, which he lost only out of laziness. He gradually loses the dead, mechanical quality and becomes a living human being again. Real personalities arise, while the current bred mass animal must disappear.


Take the trouble to think about it, and see that you do not end up finding in the pages of your book of debts that this very commandment has been violated many times!


